//
// Every count `crate::limits::LIMIT` bounds is refused at 301, at the 301st item, with a
// message naming the limit: a struct field, a parameter, a variable a function binds, and a
// tuple literal's element.  These are all refused while the program is first read; a tuple
// TYPE is refused on the second pass, so it has a file of its own
// (`a-tuple-type-past-the-limit-is-refused.loft`).  The counts that work at 300 are
// `the-counts-within-the-limit-compile.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: none — no earlier build had these limits; 301 of each compiled (or, for the
//   tuple returned by value, crashed the interpreter: see
//   `a-returned-value-past-255-bytes-arrives-whole.loft`).
//
